<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_FuelSnows                                  UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-21
    UMBRA_IS_A_REGION_NOT_A_BIOME_1. Successor to `RUT_Umbra` (BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1,
    2026-09-09), retired by this item on the owner's ruling: "Umbra is a region not a
    biome." (BENCH question card, 2026-09-21, verbatim.) Full sheet: design/Jawa/
    worldbuilding/biomes/the_propane_lakes.md (FROZEN) — unchanged by this rename; the
    sheet describes the antistellar cap's regime, this def is just correctly named now
    that "Umbra" itself names the REGION (a WorldFeature, `ashkarr_paint.py` line ~851,
    already live on the canonical save — verified this pass, not re-authored).

    🔴 BIOME-MAPPING DECISION (this item's own call, spec step 2): the cap's energy
    regime — fuel snow, ammonia flats, aurora, cold hydrocarbon/ammonia chemistry, no
    icy dayside analog — matches NO existing owned BiomeDef. Checked `RUT_NightsideIce`
    specifically (the only other nightside-cold biome we own): it is the opposite
    regime by design (no precipitation, no wildlife, no weather at all, silent/dead
    interior per nightside_ice.md §6) — the two cannot merge. So this needed a
    genuinely new BiomeDef; since the old `RUT_Umbra` content already WAS that new
    biome (fully authored: terrain, weather, wildAnimals, wildPlants, diseases), the
    entire mechanics content below is carried forward UNCHANGED from `RUT_Umbra.xml` —
    only the defName, label and this header comment change. Nothing here is new
    "mechanics kit" work; it's the existing content correctly re-labelled.

    Name chosen to keep the flavour ("it snows fuel" §1; "fuel snow" is the sheet's own
    reflavoring of SnowGentle/SnowHard, see the weather note below) while not reusing
    "Umbra", which now names the region. Stays under `RUT_` / UtinniPatches — the wider
    `biome_mod_architecture.md` migration wave (RUT_ -> standalone RM_ mods) has not
    reached this biome yet and doing that split is explicitly out of this item's scope;
    when that wave does reach it, add a row for `RUT_FuelSnows` there.

    🔴 KNOWN CONSEQUENCE, recorded rather than hidden: `RUT_Umbra` is NOT a zero-tile
    biome — BIOME_WORLD_SWITCH_WAVE_1 (2026-09-12, commit f90d660ae) already painted it
    live onto 2,531 real world tiles on the canonical save
    (`CANONICAL_ASHKARR_START_2026-09-12.rws` / the frozen `world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_
    tiles.csv`, both as of that date — a live re-read may differ, never re-derive this
    number from the CSV as current). Retiring `RUT_Umbra`'s defName without a live
    repaint (explicitly out of scope for this item — "the planet is painted once, at
    the end") leaves those tiles' stored biome shortHash unresolvable until the
    terminal repaint absorbs the rename, per the owner's own stated policy on this
    exact tradeoff ([[world-remake-is-the-last-step]]: "do the clean thing and let the
    remake absorb the divergence"). This is a deliberate, recorded consequence, not an
    oversight — flagged here and in `infrastructure/state/facts/biome_paint_list.md` so
    the terminal repaint's author knows this defName changed since the last live paint.

    Everything below this line is verbatim from `RUT_Umbra.xml` except defName/label:

    Replaces the donor `AB_PropaneLakes` (Alpha Biomes) on its LAND tiles only — the
    lake itself is a separate, already-owned worldmap water biome, `RUT_PropaneLake`
    (57 tiles, `LIQUID_BIOMES_MAP_1`, paint DONE per that sheet's Owed).

    MEASURED (sheet SS0, 2026-09-06 export): 2,531 tiles, arc 132-179 (sun 49-76 deg
    below horizon), temp p10/median/p90 -73.0/-62.2/-47.8 C - the coldest LAND on the
    planet. Regions Deadstone/Umbra/Ammonia Flats (region names, distinct from this
    def's own identity now).

    Weather: SS4b and ban 3 rule this directly - "Aurora-clear - the common state. No
    visibility blockage (owner): starlight and curtain-light; ranged fire works; the
    sky is the most beautiful on the planet." Fog/Rain/RainyThunderstorm/FoggyRain all
    zeroed (ban 3 + ban 7 no rain, R-H1); Clear made dominant. SnowGentle/SnowHard kept
    high, reflavored per the sheet as "fuel snow" (SS4b, hydrocarbon/ammonia
    precipitation feeding the crystal flora) - not literal water snow, same
    reskin-in-place pattern The Rot's sheet uses for its own weather. DryThunderstorm
    kept low ("dry lightning over a fuel field," SS4b) - ban 4 requires ignition to
    need a hot source or spark, so this stays rare, never dominant.

    animalDensity/plantDensity/diseaseMtbDays kept at the donor's own values (sheet
    SS0 "Donor inventory taken in" lists these as read-in, not disputed).

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/the_propane_lakes.json. Ban 1 (no icy
    dayside analogs) and ban 2 (no kyber) are both roster-level bans already
    enforced by that JSON's own evictions, not re-checked field-by-field here.

    NOT this pass's scope: `ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1` (the sealed lab beneath the lake);
    the electrojet tap building; the crater-event map permanence; the island
    landmark (tile 5873); any world repaint (paint already DONE for the lake per
    the sheet's Owed — this def is the land only, un-painted by THIS item).

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_FuelSnows</defName>
    <label>the Fuel Snows</label>
    <description>The far end of the world: a black sea of liquid fuel under the brightest sky on the planet, ringed by frozen ammonia flats. It snows fuel. The aurora is the strongest anywhere -- the magnetosphere slamming back together after its rude shock upstream -- so the ice glows green and violet even without a moon. The fast things run in blue flame, because nothing moves fluidly here without burning; the plants are crystal, and grow overnight from what falls.</description>
    <workerClass>AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_PropaneLakes</workerClass>

    <!-- OWNER RULING 2026-09-19 (RUT_UMBRA_ROADS_RULING_1): the ban STANDS. No
         roads in the Fuel Snows, same as RUT_ExtremeDesert's "No roads through the deep
         dune". This flag was previously an unexamined default with no sheet behind
         it; it is now ruled and the sheet says so.
         MEASURED (2026-09-07 link export): 42 tiles carry stored road links,
         and 74 of their 78 links run internally - only 4 leave the region. So
         the ban costs almost no connectivity: it hides an internal web in the
         coldest land on the planet, not a route to anywhere.
         Nothing is destroyed by this. `potentialRoads` keeps every link in the
         world data (2,470 across the planet, unchanged); the flag only decides
         whether they DRAW. Flipping this to true restores all 42 tiles with no
         re-authoring, should the Assailant/Rakata-vault pilgrimage ever want a
         road in. -->
    <allowRoads>false</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.75</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_PropaneLakes</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>110</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_PackedSnow</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.87</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_PackedIce</terrain>
        <min>0.87</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>70</Clear>
      <SnowGentle>20</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>25</SnowHard>
      <DryThunderstorm>2</DryThunderstorm>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_Frostmite MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.35</AA_Frostmite>  <!-- frostmite - small — corpse-sweeper, the pole's undertaker, keep -->
      <AA_FrostboundBehemoth MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.126</AA_FrostboundBehemoth>  <!-- frostbound behemoth - huge — ammonia life of the Flats, keep -->
      <AA_Terramorph MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Terramorph>  <!-- terramorph - medium — Flats mineral chemistry, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Slurrypede MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.02</AA_Slurrypede>  <!-- slurrypede - lab fauna — the containment facility's feeder, still running, adjust-keep -->
      <RUT_BurnerAscendant>0.03</RUT_BurnerAscendant>  <!-- the Burners, ascendant — apex of the Blue Desert's line (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1, §4) -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <AB_CrystalHorn>1.0</AB_CrystalHorn>  <!-- crystal horn -->
      <AB_FrostLeaf>0.6</AB_FrostLeaf>  <!-- frost leaf -->
      <AB_RimeNodules>0.4</AB_RimeNodules>  <!-- rime nodules -->
      <!-- SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner review 2026-09-20: AB_CrystalFlower moved OUT
           (kept only at poison_forest, its "elsewhere") and PoisonShrub moved IN from
           wasteland (".8 cells, propane lakes"). Both rulings landed in
           rosters/the_propane_lakes.json and reached the game only through
           BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml's now-retired replace operation; transplanted here by
           BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1. -->
      <PoisonShrub>0.35</PoisonShrub>  <!-- poison shrub -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>1</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
